{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S1 T2 rebased onto current origin/main 8cd6e6ec03 (10 commits of drift) and re-pushed as PATCH SET 2 of Gerrit 1885 - 'updated: 1', so the Change-Id I2f464a52 was preserved this time (the earlier lesson applied). Prior Verified -1 on patch set 1 resolved as follows: the first failure was a single test out of 14009, tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py::test_session_finish_fails_explicitly_when_porcelain_times_out, macOS/py3.13 only. I did NOT blind-retry. Investigated and found it is a KNOWN pre-existing macOS timing flake with two tracked tickets - 9bb7-4430-1202-4d93 tapestried-abhorrent-tuna (closed) records the identical test failing on an unrelated change Gerrit 1869 PS1, and fb03-2609-ef83-4b41 asbestos-popular-tench (in_progress) owns the remaining fix and names this exact mode: the inner 5s git watchdog fires as designed but the harness outer 12s deadline expires first under macOS runner load, so the ORACLE WINDOW fails, not the code. It passes locally (12 passed) and shares no code path with binding persistence. Posted a recheck stating that reasoning per CONTRIBUTING.md section 6; that run was then cancelled/superseded, and the rebase gives CI a fresh current-base run anyway. COORDINATOR CORRECTION ABSORBED - this changes S2: RP-04 S7.1 landed a SECOND config gate. scripts/check_config_ownership.py and scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py now exist and Makefile runs BOTH gates in make lint, so they are in the pre-commit hook AND in Verified. Verified locally: config-ownership exit 0, make lint exit 0, typecheck 565 files. The registry's LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS are (relpath, symbol, rationale) tuples keyed on PATH+SYMBOL, and I confirmed entries exist for binding_store.py + os.environ.get (rationale cites L110, the _env_int site) and binding_store.py + RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE (cites L538). CONSEQUENCE FOR S2: moving _env_int and that env read into binding_lifecycle.py creates an UNREGISTERED path+symbol pair, so make lint will fail and BLOCK THE COMMIT before any push. S2 must add binding_lifecycle.py entries in the SAME change, with a rationale naming the move and pointing at RP-04 S7.3.a as the eventual seam owner, and retarget/remove the stale binding_store.py entries so the registry stays truthful - while still preserving the ambient sourcing byte-identically rather than cutting it to a seam. scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py is NOT in RP-02's recorded file_impact, so it must be added to brainy-cooked-hog via set-file-impact and noted in ADR 0099. T2 itself needs no registry change: _env_int never moved, it stayed in binding_store.py."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787105456683297001,"uuid":"3a21582a-4128-4746-bd6f-2569bd32e649"}